post_install() {
    cat <<EOF
==> micdroid installed.

Launch it from your application menu ("Micdroid"), or run: micdroid-tray

The background service is NOT started or enabled at login automatically -
the tray app starts it on demand the first time you actually use it, so it
costs nothing while you're not using the feature. If you'd rather it also
runs at login:
    systemctl --user enable --now micdroid.service

First-time device setup: on your phone, Settings > Developer options >
Wireless debugging > "Pair device with pairing code", then use "Pair new
device" in the app.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    post_install
}
